\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {9}{\ignorespaces The same flood as a stack of time layers in $(x,y,t)$. Each translucent sheet is one layer's reachable set (Fig.\nobreakspace  {}8\hbox {} collapsed to a single instant); the dotted line is the moving obstacle's own trajectory traced through time, i.e.\ the exclusion tube each layer's notch is a cross-section of. A route that stays on one side of the tube throughout is one homotopy class; a route that crosses to the other side is distinct under Eq.\nobreakspace  {}21\hbox {}.}}{13}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:spacetime-flood-volume}{{9}{13}}
